From 6e51f01070e9ba4c1907244c094e555e419d11ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:27:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 037/125] urltest: fallbacks, taken in their order while no
 outbound answers

A urltest group had no way to say "these only when the others are down":
every member competed by delay. The option fallbacks lists outbounds the group
selects only while none of outbounds is a candidate (no test result, or held
back by the download test): the first one in the list that is, regardless of
the delays and the tolerance. As soon as an outbound has a result again the
group returns to it, an earlier fallback is taken back the same way, and a
fallback in use does not seed the tolerance against the outbounds.

The fallbacks are tested with the outbounds in every round, so their state is
known before it is needed, the Clash API shows their delays, and what the group
learns from traffic (failed dials, connections without an answer) and the
download test work for them as for any member. All() and the dependencies list
the outbounds, then the fallbacks: the outbound manager starts them first and
reports an unknown tag or a cycle. A fallback that repeats a tag is an error;
without the option nothing changes.
